====Verb====
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|obsolete|intransitive|hunting}} To release a new set of [[hound]]s. {{defdate|15th-17th c.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|now|_|rare}} To [[place]] (people or horses) in relays, such that one can take over from another. {{defdate|from 18th c.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive|now|_|rare}} To take on a new relay of [[horse]]s; to change horses. {{defdate|from 19th c.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[pass on]] or [[transfer]] (information). {{defdate|from 19th c.}}
#: {{ux|en|The CCTV cameras '''relay''' what's going on to the headquarters.}}
#: {{ux|en|Can you '''relay''' this message to John?}}

